# Cumulus 01 Reference Set

Generated on 2026-07-27 with the built-in image generation tool.

These images are opaque visual references for Blender modeling and Unreal
volumetric-cloud look development. They are not runtime textures, density
maps, masks, or Base Color inputs.

## Images

### `REF_Cumulus01_Hero_Keyframe.png`

- Purpose: primary silhouette, mood, color, and lighting target.
- Resolution: 1672 x 941.
- Use the broad flat base, tall asymmetric central tower, and large value
  separation as the primary art-direction target.
- Do not reproduce the visible micro-lobes in the Blender source mesh. Those
  details belong to the Unreal erosion/noise pass.

### `REF_Cumulus01_Modeling_Views.png`

- Purpose: front, side, and three-quarter Blender modeling reference.
- Resolution: 1672 x 941.
- Model approximately 10 to 16 major rounded masses.
- Preserve the broad front profile, narrow side profile, asymmetric crown,
  and nearly flat common base.
- Treat the sheet as a design guide rather than a mathematically consistent
  orthographic turnaround.

### `REF_Cumulus01_Lighting_Keys.png`

- Purpose: Unreal lighting and time-of-day comparison.
- Resolution: 2048 x 768.
- Left: clear midday.
- Center: late-afternoon backlight; primary target for the first material.
- Right: sunset side light.
- Match large light and shadow groups before adding fine erosion detail.

## Prompt Set

The prompts intentionally describe the requested qualities of a luminous
contemporary Japanese animated feature background without imitating a
specific artist or existing film.

### Hero keyframe

```text
Create one majestic, isolated summer cumulus cloud for a contemporary
Japanese animated feature-film sky. Use a pristine cobalt-to-cyan sky, a
broad nearly flat condensation base, one dominant central mass, stacked
rounded lobes, a few smaller upward-growing turrets, and a slightly
asymmetric crown. Show the complete uncropped cloud from a low angle with
generous blue-sky margins. Use radiant late-afternoon backlight, restrained
silver lining, warm ivory and pale-peach highlights, and a cool cyan to
blue-violet underside. Premium hand-painted digital animation background,
stylized rather than photorealistic, with large readable value groups.
Exactly one cloud; no scenery, people, birds, aircraft, text, logo, or
watermark.
```

### Modeling views

```text
Using the approved hero cloud as the design reference, create a clean
three-view modeling sheet: front, side, and three-quarter. Preserve the flat
base, tall central tower, asymmetric crown, and overall proportions while
simplifying the surface into about 10 to 16 large rounded masses suitable for
Blender and a 128-cubed SDF. Use neutral diffuse daylight on a uniform pale
sky-blue background. Keep each view complete, evenly spaced, equally scaled,
and aligned to the same baseline. No labels, borders, measurements, scenery,
extra fragments, text, or watermark.
```

### Lighting keys

```text
Create a three-panel lighting study of the approved single cumulus design.
Keep silhouette, camera, scale, flat base, and major lobes as consistent as
possible. Panel one is clear midday with a cool-white top and soft blue
underside. Panel two is late-afternoon backlight with warm ivory and
pale-peach highlights, restrained silver lining, cobalt sky, and blue-violet
base. Panel three is sunset side light with coral-apricot edges, lavender and
indigo shadow masses, and an orange-to-violet sky. Use premium hand-painted
contemporary Japanese animation background qualities, stylized rather than
photorealistic. No labels, borders, scenery, extra clouds, text, or watermark.
```

## Production Interpretation

For the first Blender asset, use the modeling sheet for geometry and the
center panel of the lighting sheet for Unreal look development. The hero
keyframe remains the final visual target. Any mismatch between the three
views should be resolved in favor of a watertight, readable silhouette and a
flat cloud base.
